manifest_item.statement:
In branch (CP) of the regime of [[def-nondegenerate-root-of-unity-level-one-hecke-regime]], for every $\lambda\in RP_\alpha$ and every partition $\mu$ of content $\alpha$, the graded decomposition polynomial factors as $$[S(\mu):D(\lambda)]_q=\sum_{
u\in RP_\alpha}a_{\lambda,
u}(q)\,d_{
u,\mu}(q),$$ where $a_{\lambda,
u}$ are the adjustment polynomials of [[def-graded-adjustment-polynomials-in-positive-characteristic]] and $d_{
u,\mu}$ the characteristic-independent global-basis transition polynomial of [[def-level-one-global-basis-transition-polynomials-in-the-symmetric-group-convention]]; equivalently $[J(
u)]=[D(
u)]+\sum_{\lambda\lhd
u}a_{\lambda,
u}(q)[D(\lambda)]$. In particular the characteristic-$p$ decomposition matrix is the product of the dominance-unitriangular adjustment matrix and the (characteristic-independent) matrix of global-basis coefficients, and no claim is made that the adjustment matrix is the identity. Choice is inherited only through the transported global-basis suppliers.

